From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 16:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mount: fstab: add explicit (void) to parameterless function
 definitions

mtab_is_writable(), read_mounttable(), read_procmounts() and
read_fstab() were defined using old K&R-style empty parentheses,
which historically meant "unspecified arguments" rather than "no
arguments". C23 changes empty parentheses on a function definition
to explicitly mean zero arguments, and recent Clang versions warn
about the old form being deprecated, which nfs-utils' unconditional
-Werror=strict-prototypes turns into a hard build error.

None of these functions take arguments and none are called with
any, so adding the explicit (void) parameter list is a no-op change
in behavior that matches what the code already assumed.

Signed-off-by: Sid Manning <atx0x200@gmail.com>
---
 utils/mount/fstab.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/utils/mount/fstab.c b/utils/mount/fstab.c
index 3eda7d343..0bcd9552d 100644
--- a/utils/mount/fstab.c
+++ b/utils/mount/fstab.c
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@
 }
 
 int
-mtab_is_writable() {
+mtab_is_writable(void) {
 	int fd;
 
 	/* Should we write to /etc/mtab upon an update?
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@
  * Return 0 on success.
  */
 static void
-read_mounttable() {
+read_mounttable(void) {
         mntFILE *mfp;
         const char *fnam;
         struct mntentchn *mc = &mounttable;
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@
  * Return 0 on success.
  */
 static void
-read_procmounts() {
+read_procmounts(void) {
         mntFILE *mfp;
         const char *fnam;
         struct mntentchn *mc = &procmounts;
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
 }
 
 static void
-read_fstab()
+read_fstab(void)
 {
 	mntFILE *mfp = NULL;
 	const char *fnam;
--
2.46.2
